ing different angles and expressions. The system accepts up to 80 photos total. For optimal results, maintain a resolution of \"960px or higher per photo for best quality.\" Avoid sunglasses, masks, or extreme expressions, as these reduce reference data quality.\n\n## Character Creation and Training\n\nOnce photos are uploaded, the training process takes \"3 to 5 minutes\" and costs 25 credits (approximately $1.25). Rather than simply matching a single reference image, Soul ID builds an internalized model. The system analyzes facial structure, hair, posture, and expression patterns to create a digital twin that understands the person's core identity rather than copying a snapshot.\n\n## Reuse Across Content\n\nA trained Soul ID avatar can be deployed across both image and video generation indefinitely. The same identity applies automatically to every project without retraining. Creators select from \"20+ built-in looks (editorial, retro, Y2K, and more)\" style presets to define tone while maintaining character consistency.\n\n## UI Steps\n\nThe process follows this workflow:\n1. Upload reference photos\n2. Train the avatar (system processes the images)\n3. Select style presets\n4. Generate content using the avatar\n5. Reuse and scale across platforms","durationMs":5470,"url":"https://higgsfield.ai/blog/sould-id-best-character-consistency"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbaff355-c6b6-48dc-9679-4af70bdde1b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_cowork","cwd":"/home/claude","sessionId":"f6c49162-7b81-5373-a7c1-f58edfefee41","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"swirling-plotting-octopus"}
{"parentUuid":"d1662aed-ed92-4de4-9f9a-2f66c336a4a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eea1a00a-fa8d-4ce0-963d-d0f411062aaf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014fC4FTY3w55iiUiBC4D28e","type":"tool_result","content":"# Higgsfield AI Workflow Overview\n\nBased on the available documentation, here's what the platform offers:\n\n## Cinema Studio 3.5\nThe primary production environment features an \"AI Director function [that] takes a creative concept and breaks it into individual shots.\" Users then apply \"per-shot camera controls\" for directorial movements like dollies, trucks, pans, and tilts. The system supports \"collaborative editing elements\" for team-based projects.\n\n## Character Consistency\nThe Soul ID system lets creators \"define a character from a reference image and carry that identity consistently across subsequent generations.\" The Multi Reference tool lets you establish multiple visual anchors before generating content.\n\n## Creative Tools & Post-Production\nBeyond Cinema Studio, the platform provides \"more than 80 purpose-built creative tools\" including face swapping, lipsync work, and headshot generation. Post-production capabilities include brush-based inpainting, video-level edits, upscaling, background removal, and color grading.\n\n## Model Integration\nThe system integrates multiple AI models including \"Seedance 2.0, Kling 3.0, Wan 2.6, Veo 3, Sora 2\" and others, with the roster updating as new models emerge.\n\n**Note:** The documentation doesn't detail specific project/library workflow steps or clip extension procedures beyond these general capabilities."}]},"uuid":"38932f57-886e-49f2-a18b-0c32233b7c32","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:17:59.749Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":3390,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Higgsfield AI Workflow Overview\n\nBased on the available documentation, here's what the platform offers:\n\n## Cinema Studio 3.5\nThe primary production environment features an \"AI Director function [that] takes a creative concept and breaks it into individual shots.\" Users then apply \"per-shot camera controls\" for directorial movements like dollies, trucks, pans, and tilts. The system supports \"collaborative editing elements\" for team-based projects.\n\n## Character Consistency\nThe Soul ID system lets creators \"define a character from a reference image and carry that identity consistently across subsequent generations.\" The Multi Reference tool lets you establish multiple visual anchors before generating content.\n\n## Creative Tools & Post-Production\nBeyond Cinema Studio, the platform provides \"more than 80 purpose-built creative tools\" including face swapping, lipsync work, and headshot generation. Post-production capabilities include brush-based inpainting, video-level edits, upscaling, background removal, and color grading.\n\n## Model Integration\nThe system integrates multiple AI models including \"Seedance 2.0, Kling 3.0, Wan 2.6, Veo 3, Sora 2\" and others, with the roster updating as new models emerge.\n\n**Note:** The documentation doesn't detail specific project/library workflow steps or clip extension procedures beyond these general capabilities.","durationMs":4390,"url":"https://geo.higgsfield.ai/higgsfield-ai-features-full-guide-2026"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d1662aed-ed92-4de4-9f9a-2f66c336a4a6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_cowork","cwd":"/home/claude","sessionId":"f6c49162-7b81-5373-a7c1-f58edfefee41","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"swirling-plotting-octopus"}
{"parentUuid":"d2a43015-c2b4-429f-8e97-0e47639531a5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eea1a00a-fa8d-4ce0-963d-d0f411062aaf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnqYfZg94SD4vXsjXvVGBg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Recent Runway Web App Features\n\n**Workflows** — Node-based system allowing users to \"chain together multiple models, modalities and intermediary steps for even more control of your generations.\"\n\n**Aleph 2.0** — Video editing model that lets users \"edit a frame the way you want, and Aleph 2.0 edits the rest of your video to match.\"\n\n**Gen-4.5** — Described as \"the world's best video model,\" supporting text-to-video and image-to-video generation with first frame control.\n\n**References** — Allows generating \"consistent characters, locations and more\" using multimodal inputs across multiple reference images.\n\n**Keyframes** — Control feature enabling users to supply \"first and last frame inputs\" plus middle keyframes for precise movement direction in video generation.\n\n**Extend/Expand Video** — Extends generations to longer durations or \"transform videos into new aspect ratios by generating new areas around your input video.\"\n\n**Act-Two** — Motion capture model offering \"major improvements in generation quality and support for head, face, body and hand tracking.\"\n\n**Timeline/Studio** — Editor letting users \"trim, stitch, reorder and export a final video\" within a unified interface.\n\n**Projects/Assets** — Organizational system for storing and managing generated images and videos with tagging, favoriting, and bulk action capabilities."}]},"uuid":"461c63b7-7b8d-4067-8ecd-c781a926a1a5","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:18:02.508Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":36046,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Recent Runway Web App Features\n\n**Workflows** — Node-based system allowing users to \"chain together multiple models, modalities and intermediary steps for even more control of your generations.\"\n\n**Aleph 2.0** — Video editing model that lets users \"edit a frame the way you want, and Aleph 2.0 edits the rest of your video to match.\"\n\n**Gen-4.5** — Described as \"the world's best video model,\" supporting text-to-video and image-to-video generation with first frame control.\n\n**References** — Allows generating \"consistent characters, locations and more\" using multimodal inputs across multiple reference images.\n\n**Keyframes** — Control feature enabling users to supply \"first and last frame inputs\" plus middle keyframes for precise movement direction in video generation.\n\n**Extend/Expand Video** — Extends generations to longer durations or \"transform videos into new aspect ratios by generating new areas around your input video.\"\n\n**Act-Two** — Motion capture model offering \"major improvements in generation quality and support for head, face, body and hand tracking.\"\n\n**Timeline/Studio** — Editor letting users \"trim, stitch, reorder and export a final video\" within a unified interface.\n\n**Projects/Assets** — Organizational system for storing and managing generated images and videos with tagging, favoriting, and bulk action capabilities.","durationMs":4896,"url":"https://runway.com/changelog"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d2a43015-c2b4-429f-8e97-0e47639531a5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_cowork","cwd":"/home/claude","sessionId":"f6c49162-7b81-5373-a7c1-f58edfefee41","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"swirling-plotting-octopus"}
{"parentUuid":"e2d29311-a78f-45c1-86c3-1d33ed6cf8df","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eea1a00a-fa8d-4ce0-963d-d0f411062aaf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bZztZGeWXa3ctFRJn9YVX","type":"tool_result","content":"# Runway Dev API Capabilities\n\n## Video Models\nThe platform supports numerous video generation models including:\n- **Gen-4.5**: Text-to-video and image-to-video (2-10 seconds)\n- **Seedance 2.5**: Text, image, or video input (4-30 seconds at 480p/720p, 1080p support)\n- **Seedance 2.0**: High-quality generation with keyframe control (4-15 seconds)\n- **Aleph 2.0**: Video editing via text prompts and keyframe images\n- **Grok Imagine Video 1.5**: Text or image-based generation (1-15 seconds)\n- **Hailuo 3.0**: Keyframe and reference support (5-15 seconds)\n- **WAN 3.0**: Native audio generation (up to 30 seconds)\n\n## Image Generation\nModels include GPT Image 2.5 (Flare/Sunburst), Seedream 5.0 Pro/Lite, Grok Imagine Image 2, and Gemini 3 Pro Image.\n\n## Key Parameters & Constraints\n\n**Video parameters:**\n- Duration ranges vary by model (typically 2-30 seconds)\n- Resolutions: 480p, 720p, 1080p, 4K options\n- Aspect ratios: Multiple fixed options (16:9, 9:16, 1:1, etc.)\n- Keyframe support on select models\n\n**Image-to-Video:**\n- \"Durations from 4–15 seconds\" for Seedance 2.0\n- Aspect ratio preservation on some models\n- Reference image support (up to 30 images on Seedance 2.5)\n\n## Audio & Enhancement\n- Text-to-speech (ElevenLabs v3, Multilingual v2)\n- Sound effects generation\n- Voice dubbing and audio isolation\n- Frame rate enhancement (24-120 fps)\n\n## Professional Features\n- HDR output formats (HDR10, HLG, ProRes, OpenEXR)\n- Model Router for automated selection\n- Content moderation settings"}]},"uuid":"a9197e96-b1cd-4aab-a3c4-4fa95b1f72fa","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:18:03.818Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":49657,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Runway Dev API Capabilities\n\n## Video Models\nThe platform supports numerous video generation models including:\n- **Gen-4.5**: Text-to-video and image-to-video (2-10 seconds)\n- **Seedance 2.5**: Text, image, or video input (4-30 seconds at 480p/720p, 1080p support)\n- **Seedance 2.0**: High-quality generation with keyframe control (4-15 seconds)\n- **Aleph 2.0**: Video editing via text prompts and keyframe images\n- **Grok Imagine Video 1.5**: Text or image-based generation (1-15 seconds)\n- **Hailuo 3.0**: Keyframe and reference support (5-15 seconds)\n- **WAN 3.0**: Native audio generation (up to 30 seconds)\n\n## Image Generation\nModels include GPT Image 2.5 (Flare/Sunburst), Seedream 5.0 Pro/Lite, Grok Imagine Image 2, and Gemini 3 Pro Image.\n\n## Key Parameters & Constraints\n\n**Video parameters:**\n- Duration ranges vary by model (typically 2-30 seconds)\n- Resolutions: 480p, 720p, 1080p, 4K options\n- Aspect ratios: Multiple fixed options (16:9, 9:16, 1:1, etc.)\n- Keyframe support on select models\n\n**Image-to-Video:**\n- \"Durations from 4–15 seconds\" for Seedance 2.0\n- Aspect ratio preservation on some models\n- Reference image support (up to 30 images on Seedance 2.5)\n\n## Audio & Enhancement\n- Text-to-speech (ElevenLabs v3, Multilingual v2)\n- Sound effects generation\n- Voice dubbing and audio isolation\n- Frame rate enhancement (24-120 fps)\n\n## Professional Features\n- HDR output formats (HDR10, HLG, ProRes, OpenEXR)\n- Model Router for automated selection\n- Content moderation settings","durationMs":7284,"url":"https://docs.dev.runwayml.com/api-details/api_changelog/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2d29311-a78f-45c1-86c3-1d33ed6cf8df","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_cowork","cwd":"/home/claude","sessionId":"f6c49162-7b81-5373-a7c1-f58edfefee41","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"swirling-plotting-octopus"}
